from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
p=r/'README.md'
s=p.read_text()
old='Use **HOME** to cycle the main oscillator pages, **SELECT** to browse settings/options and **SEL** to confirm.'
assert old in s
s=s.replace(old,'Use **HOME** to cycle the main oscillator pages. On any ordinary screen where SELECT has no dedicated function, turning **SELECT** opens the exact same screen list as on PLAY. Where SELECT already controls a step, FX selection, slot, scroll position or setting, that function remains unchanged. **SEL** confirms selections. Protected update, recovery and welcome screens are excluded from the global navigation shortcut.')
s=s.replace('- **PLAY:** Main CXS/SAW oscillator. The four knobs control PRESSURE/BALANCE/MEMORY/DENSITY in CXS, and BRIGHT/EDGE/BODY/LEVEL in SAW.','- **PLAY:** Main CXS/SAW oscillator. The four knobs control PRESSURE/BALANCE/MEMORY/DENSITY in CXS, and BRIGHT/EDGE/BODY/LEVEL in SAW. In SAW mode, the BRIGHT range now starts with a warmer, filtered bass core; EDGE and the four SOUND SHAPE controls still provide aggressive sounds when deliberately raised. For rounded bass, start around BRIGHT 35–60, EDGE 40–55, with a low-pass/ladder filter and moderate resonance. This evokes the role of an analog bass synth without reproducing a specific hardware instrument.')
s=s.replace('- **FX / EDIT:** Effects and channel EQ.','- **FX / EDIT:** Effects and channel EQ. REVERB offers SPRING (short, bright), HALL (longer tail) and ROOM (controlled short ambience) tonal presets of the shared reverb engine. Turn K1 to select a type, K2 DECAY, K3 SIZE and K4 MIX. MIX 0 is the unchanged dry sound; MIX 100 is the reverb return only (not a volume control). The return has been gain-balanced to stay audible even fully wet. The reverb still uses the same shared memory/taps and does not add an extra processor per voice.')
s=s.replace('`RUPTURE-V1.76.fwsc`','`RUPTURE-V1.77.fwsc`')
p.write_text(s)
p=r/'CHEAT-SHEET.html';s=p.read_text();anchor='<section><h2>PLAY & HOME</h2>'
assert anchor in s
s=s.replace(anchor,'<section><h2>SELECT: GLOBAL SCREEN LIST</h2><p>On any regular screen where SELECT is not otherwise assigned, turn SELECT to open the same screen list as PLAY. If SELECT already chooses a SEQ step, FX entry, settings row, project slot, name position or HELP card, that behavior is preserved. The shortcut never interrupts OTA, recovery or the first-run wizard.</p></section>\n'+anchor)
anchor='<section><h2>V1.48 SAW HARMONIC GUARD</h2>'
assert anchor in s
s=s.replace(anchor,'<section><h2>SAW BASS (V1.77)</h2><p>SAW BRIGHT now gives more usable warm, lower-harmonic sound through the middle of its range. For a round bass voice, use BRIGHT 35–60, EDGE about 50, WEIGHT modest, BITE/PUNCH low, then shape with the resonant ladder filter and ADSR. Raise BRIGHT/EDGE/BITE for aggressive grit. No second oscillator or audio-rate filter was added.</p></section>\n<section><h2>REVERB TYPES AND TRUE WET MIX</h2><p>FX → REVERB: K1 selects SPRING, HALL or ROOM tonal presets, K2 sets DECAY, K3 SIZE and K4 MIX. Each type has different length, early reflections and density from the existing global tank. MIX 0 is dry only, MIX 100 is wet only; more MIX is not simply a master-volume reduction. No extra effect buffer or per-voice processor is used.</p></section>\n'+anchor)
p.write_text(s)
p=r/'CHANGELOG.md';s=p.read_text();p.write_text('''# RUPTURE V1.77 — Navigation, Warm SAW & Usable Reverb\n\n- SELECT on a normal screen with no assigned SELECT behavior now opens the identical scrolling screen list used on PLAY. Dedicated SELECT functions for FX, SEQ, project/sequence slots, help, settings and safe dialogs remain unchanged; no interception during OTA/recovery/welcome.\n- SAW oscillator timbre: the original one-pole low-state and bandlimited SAW are retained. Rebalanced BRIGHT response puts a warmer filtered bass core in the lower/middle travel, while EDGE and SOUND SHAPE are less prone to premature hard clipping. No extra oscillator, delay line, wavetable or filter state. The original CXS oscillator code is untouched.\n- Reverb: SPRING, HALL and ROOM tonal presets use more distinct SIZE/DECAY values and expanded existing tap spacing. A much more audible five-tap wet return, with stable 0% dry / 100% wet endpoints, fixes the perceived volume-drop-only behavior. The existing single 4096-sample tank, five reads and stereo return path remain in place; no per-voice reverb or larger buffers. These are character presets within the same algorithm, not separate physical spring and hall simulations.\n- Builds and host regression/measurement results are in `docs/TEST-RESULTS-V1.77.md`. No project storage-layout change, firmware identity change, bootheader change or trusted OTA loader change. Hardware listening/CPU/DMA verification is still required.\n\n'''+s)
p=r/'WEBSITE-DEPLOY.md';s=p.read_text().replace('V1.75','V1.77');p.write_text(s)
